      Medicare Part D Penalty Calculator
    </h1>
    <p class="partd-hero-date">Figures last verified against official sources in July 2026.</p>
    
    <div style="background: #0A3D3A; border-radius: 0.75rem; padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; margin: 0.75rem 0 1rem;">
      <p style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: #C9933A; margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;">Quick Answer</p>
      <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: #ffffff; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">The Medicare Part D late enrollment penalty is 1% of the national base beneficiary premium ($36.78 in 2026) multiplied by the number of full months you went without creditable drug coverage. This penalty is permanent and added to your monthly Part D premium for as long as you have Medicare.</p>
    </div>

    <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0.75rem 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;">
      <li style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem; color: #4B5A6E;"><span aria-hidden="true" style="color: #0A3D3A; font-weight: 700; flex-shrink: 0;">→</span> Adults who went without Medicare drug coverage for more than 63 consecutive days and want to calculate the permanent Part D late enrollment penalty before they enroll.</li>
      <li style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem; color: #4B5A6E;"><span aria-hidden="true" style="color: #0A3D3A; font-weight: 700; flex-shrink: 0;">→</span> Retirees comparing the cost of their penalty surcharge against the cost of choosing a Part D plan to determine the most cost-effective path forward.</li>
      <li style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem; color: #4B5A6E;"><span aria-hidden="true" style="color: #0A3D3A; font-weight: 700; flex-shrink: 0;">→</span> Medicare beneficiaries who believe they had creditable drug coverage from an employer or VA and want to confirm whether it eliminates their penalty.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="partd-hero-sub">
      Calculate your permanent Medicare Part D prescription drug surcharge instantly. Free — no signup, no account, no email required. All calculations run in your browser and are never stored.
    </p>
    <p class="partd-hero-source">
      Based on official 2026 CMS formula (National Base Premium: {BASE_PREMIUM_2026}). Last reviewed: {lastReviewed}. Not affiliated with CMS or any government agency.
    </p>
